{"title": "Text-to-speech", "description": "Read text aloud or generate spoken audio using the configured voice.", "examples": ["make an audio recording of this", "read this aloud", "send a voice note"], "events": [], "tools": ["text_to_speech"]}

The administrator configures the speech model and voice (see your context); you supply the text and, only when the configured model supports them, separate delivery instructions. You may research the configured model's documented capabilities or text markup, but never choose another model or voice. No inherited context or presets. Authentication is internal: never search for API keys, install speech packages or call other speech services from the sandbox. Speech files are saved in the job workspace; this tool does not deliver them. Spending and unresolved-charge blocks are shared with llm_service. Never automatically repeat synthesis after an interruption or unknown charge; charges are reconciled automatically. If the tool fails, report the error to the admin instead of improvising an alternative.
